    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "WF2 OVERVIEW -\n## WF2 — Doc Creation & Escalation Routing\nARIA — Automated Incident Response System v2.0\n\nWORKFLOW PURPOSE:\nReceives validated Medium severity incidents from WF1.\nSends a human approval email and waits up to 30 minutes.\nOn approval: creates Google Doc, sends CTO alert (High only),\nupdates Sheets. On rejection/timeout: logs to WF3 only.\n\nNODE FLOW:\nWhen Executed by Another Workflow (from WF1)\n  → Gmail — Send Approval Request\n  → Wait — Approval Response (30 min)\n  → IF — Approved or Rejected?\n      ↓ TRUE (approved)        ↓ FALSE (rejected/timeout)\n  Google Docs — Create Report  Set — Rejection Payload\n  → Gmail — Medium Alert       → Execute WF3 Log Rejection\n  → Sheets — Mark Processed\n  → Execute WF3 Log Success\n\nDATA REFERENCE AFTER WAIT NODE:\nAll nodes after Wait must use:\n$('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.fieldname\nNOT $json.fieldname (Wait node resets $json context)\n\nRUBRIC CRITERIA COVERED:\nC1 — Structured doc from validated JSON\nC2 — continue-on-error on all nodes\nC4 — Both paths log to WF3\n\n--- STICKY 5: HUMAN APPROVAL GATE (place over Wait + IF nodes) ---\n## Human Approval Gate\n\nPOSITIONED BEFORE: Google Doc creation\nNo external action happens without human sign-off.\n\nAPPROVAL EMAIL CONTAINS:\n- Incident ID, title, severity, timestamp\n- Root cause (orange card)\n- Business impact (blue card)\n- Recommended action (green card)\n- ARIA post-mortem analysis\n- Approve and Reject buttons (n8n built-in)\n\nIF NODE CONDITION:\n$json.data.approved is true → TRUE branch\nAnything else → FALSE branch\n\nAPPROVED PATH:\n→ Google Doc created\n→ Gmail alert (Medium severity)\n→ Sheets row updated to Processed\n→ WF3 logs: processing_status = success\n             overall_run_health = HEALTHY\n\nREJECTED / TIMEOUT PATH:\n→ No document created\n→ No email sent\n→ Incident stays Pending in sheet\n→ WF3 logs: processing_status = pending_review\n             overall_run_health = PENDING REVIEW\n\nCOMMERCIAL RATIONALE:\nAI-generated reports must not fire without human\nsign-off. Auto-reject on timeout is the safe default —\nmissed email = manual triage, not silent processing.",
        "height": 496,
        "width": 576
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -832,
        -192
      ],
      "id": "d752605b-1e3b-4f28-9ae8-d8d1a750e384",
